<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Danish Asiatic Company</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1732">1732</a>–1840s</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Danish Asiatic Company was a trading company chartered in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/copenhagen">Copenhagen</a> in 1732 with a monopoly of Danish trade with Asia. Its ships sailed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guangzhou">Canton</a> for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tea">tea</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silk">silk</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/porcelain">porcelain</a> and to the Danish colony of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tharangambadi">Tranquebar</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, and it was among the most profitable enterprises of Denmark-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a> in the 18th century. Its monopoly ended in the 1770s and the company was dissolved in the 1840s.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/danish-asiatic-company.jpg" alt="Danish Asiatic Company" width="320" height="168" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Tinkaer1991 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Danish_Colonial_Merchant_Ensign_India.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
